            <div xml:id="d506">

                <pb facs="0465" n="383" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg383"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/607.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Mexican
                    Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-01-04"><hi rendition="#italic">January 4,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 374.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your excellency’s four notes, numbered 534, 535, 536, and 538, the
                    first two of which bear date of the 30th ultimo and the remaining two bearing
                    date of the 31st ultimo and the 2d instant, respectively, all of which relate to
                    alleged violations or contemplated violations of the neutrality laws of the
                    United States.</p>
                <p>In reply, I have the honor to inform your excellency that copies of these notes
                    have been sent to the appropriate authorities, for such action as may be
                    considered necessary.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.],</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
